Z||000000||Blazerguy||11-10-2001||02:04 PM||||I know that V8 Archie says that the 5 speed trans will handle upwards of 450 horsepower with caveats.  Obviously if you sidestep the clutch at full power, eventually something is going to give.<BR>My questions are:  <P>Which 5 speed will reliably handle more power?  The Muncie or the Isuzu?  <P>Is there any reputable or known places that can rebuild or beef up these transmissions?<P>It has been a couple of years since I was told how to tell the difference between the Muncie and the Isuzu.  How do you tell the difference?<P>What clutches are you all running, and how much horsepower are you producing?<P>Thanks guys.<P>Used to have an 87 GT 5 speed, kick myself for selling it.  Will have another sometime soon.<p>[This message has been edited by Blazerguy (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||1
